{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Four pillars of acacia.</b> Set into four sockets, and hooks are fixed in them, bent upward, to set upon them a rod on which the top of the curtain is looped — and the hooks are the וָוִין, for they are made like clasps. And the curtain: its length is ten cubits, for the width of the Tabernacle, and its width is ten cubits, for the height of the boards. It is spread at a third of the Tabernacle, so that from it inward is ten cubits and from it outward is twenty cubits — the Holy of Holies is thus found to be ten by ten, as it says: ״וְנָתַתָּה אֶת הַפָּרֹכֶת תַּחַת הַקְּרָסִים״ — the clasps that join the two sets of curtains of the Tabernacle. The width of one set is twenty cubits, and when spread over the roof of the Tabernacle from the entrance westward, it reaches to two-thirds of the Tabernacle; and the second set covered a third of the Tabernacle, and the excess hangs at the back to cover the boards."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:52.030417045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}